+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+// Verathos stage-boundary activation chain (VERATHOS_GGML_BOUNDARY_V1).
+//
+// Each pipeline stage runs in its own verathos-rpc-server process.  Without a
+// commitment to what crossed the RPC edge, every stage proves an isolated
+// statement over an activation of its own choosing, so a coordinator can run
+// one cheap stage, fabricate a plausible hidden state, and have the remaining
+// stages prove honest arithmetic on the fabrication.
+//
+// The hook keeps one running SHA-256 per direction over the payload bytes of
+// set_tensor (activations handed in) and get_tensor (activations handed back).
+// The coordinator forwards the bytes it read from stage k straight into stage
+// k+1, so an honest pipeline produces
+// output_boundary_root(k) == input_boundary_root(k+1).  The verifier requires
+// exactly that.
+//
+// The bytes are already in host RAM at both hooks, so this costs no extra
+// copies and no GPU synchronisation.  A boundary carries n_embd floats per
+// token, 8 KiB/token at F32 for the shipped 2048-wide model, which is under
+// half a percent of a typical request against generation time.
+//
+// Off unless VERATHOS_GGML_BOUNDARY_CAPTURE=1.  It has not been validated
+// against a live multi-box pipeline yet, and until it has, the byte streams
+// lining up on both sides of the edge is a design claim rather than a
+// measured one.
